1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,980
To fast is to hunger for more of God.

2
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:23,600
We fast to offer our whole selves, including our whole body, to God.

3
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:28,300
To grow in holiness.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,920
To amplify our prayers.

5
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:38,240
And to stand with the poor.

6
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:46,600
Fasting is one of the most essential and powerful of all the practices of Jesus.

7
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:53,440
It's an ancient discipline whose time has come.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,560
Good morning, Canvas Church.

9
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,380
Hi.

10
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:11,180
If I haven't met you yet, my name is Michelle Meeks.

11
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:13,200
I'm the children's pastor here at Canvas.

12
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:19,040
And this morning I'm beyond humbled to get to talk with you about fasting.

13
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:30,200
If you haven't been here last week, we are on a four-week sermon series and we're focusing on fasting, which, to be totally honest with you, this is by far the hardest message.

14
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:35,600
I haven't done this a lot, but this one's the hardest because it's a concept that we're not really used to.

15
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:44,760
It's a concept that I wasn't really used to, but I'm thrilled that I get to come and share with you what Jesus has been teaching me through this.

16
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,220
So before I begin, let's pray.

17
00:01:46,220 --> 00:01:54,340
Dear Heavenly Father, I thank you for the gift of fasting, for this practice that you've given us to draw closer to you.

18
00:01:54,380 --> 00:02:04,100
God, I pray that every word that comes out of my mouth will be from you and that everything that you want to be heard this morning will come through clearly.

19
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:05,520
In Jesus' name I pray.

20
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:05,760
Amen.

21
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:11,820
So before I start talking about fasting, I have a question.

22
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:15,780
How many of you have heard or seen the movie End of the Spear?

23
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,140
Anybody?

24
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:19,800
Ryan.

25
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:20,400
That's good.

26
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,340
Okay, we got a couple.

27
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,240
We got a couple.

28
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:24,420
If you haven't, it's an older movie.

29
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:27,540
It's probably like 15 years old by now.

30
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:30,720
It's a really good, powerful movie.

31
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:35,560
But I grew up in a church denomination called CMA, which stands for Christian Missionary Alliance.

32
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:39,340
So as you can imagine, missionaries were a big part of our church.

33
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:41,860
We sponsored missionaries.

34
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:43,480
I went on several missions trips.

35
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:51,080
And a story that I was taught when I was really young is the true story that the movie End of the Spear is based on.

36
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:55,580
And so it goes that there were five missionary men who were all pilots.

37
00:02:55,580 --> 00:03:02,900
And in 1956, they moved themselves and their whole families over to the Amazon area.

38
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:12,720
And their goal was to infiltrate some tribes that had never heard the gospel because they were really dangerous tribes.

39
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:17,940
So people hadn't been able to get to them to translate the Bible into their language.

40
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:18,900
They hadn't heard the gospel.

41
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:20,880
And so that was the goal of these five men.

42
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:29,660
So originally, because they knew these tribes were really dangerous, they would fly their planes really low and drop off supplies at these villages.

43
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:34,900
Almost like a truce letting them know, we are your friends.

44
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:37,860
We're here to help you, trying to break that barrier down.

45
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:47,220
But these men felt very called to land and talk with these people to get to know them.

46
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,640
They knew that it was dangerous.

47
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:54,600
They didn't even tell their supervisors that this was their plan because they knew that they'd be told no because it's too dangerous.

48
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,080
But they did it anyway.

49
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:58,600
The movie is based specifically on Nate Saint.

50
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:02,520
He's one of the five and he's kind of the lead character in the movie.

51
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:09,000
So even though they knew that they were risking their lives, they had children, they had spouses, they do this and they land.

52
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,400
And at first it goes really well.

53
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:17,640
They had learned a couple words and they use those words saying friend and peace and things like that.

54
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:18,260
And it goes well.

55
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,200
So they're so excited.

56
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:21,140
And they're like rejoicing and cheering.

57
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:27,680
And what happens though is the tribal men that they met went back and told the leader what was going on.

58
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,460
Well, the leader didn't like this very much.

59
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:32,260
And he said, oh, no, they have to go.

60
00:04:32,260 --> 00:04:42,240
So as they're rejoicing that the initial meet went well, they come back with spears and all five men end up being killed.

61
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,680
Sorry, that's a really somber start.

62
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:54,240
But if you get a chance, watch the movie because what God does with their sacrifice is amazing.

63
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:57,260
But I remember, I think I was around 10 when I heard this for the first time.

64
00:04:57,320 --> 00:05:09,360
And I remember thinking, how do you get to your walk with Jesus that you're at the place that they were at, that you're willing, no matter what the cost, to lay down your life for Jesus?

65
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:16,260
Because the most important thing to those five men were, what does Jesus want me to do?

66
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:21,400
And if I have to sacrifice my life, that's okay, because I want the gospel to be shared.

67
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,080
And the gospel is eventually shared.

68
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:23,980
I'm going to say anything else.

69
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:24,960
Watch the movie.

70
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:25,520
It's really good.

71
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,600
And like I said, it's a true story.

72
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:36,900
Actually, Nate Saint's son came to Liberty University when I was there and spoke with one of the tribal men that killed his dad.

73
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:41,480
They're, they have this relationship and it's so good.

74
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,320
You have to watch the movie.

75
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:48,020
But that story and that question of, am I there yet?

76
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:51,480
Like, am I at the point with Jesus where I would lay down my life for him?

77
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:54,000
Where I would, where that's the most important thing in my life.

78
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:59,820
It's sort of stuck with me my whole life and I check in with myself every now and then, like, all right, am I there yet?

79
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:03,020
Have I reached that level of love for Jesus?

80
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:05,920
And it's something that's like a life goal for me.

81
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:16,040
Not that I have like a death wish or something, but I really want God to be number one in my life, in every area, body, soul, and mind.

82
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:27,960
So fast forward to about four months ago, I heard a sermon about getting away for a while and this guy went and see pastor, he stays in a cabin and gets away from all life's things that bog you down.

83
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:30,400
And one of the things that he does is fasting.

84
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,980
And I remember hearing this message and it was really powerful.

85
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:36,440
And I decided that I wanted to try fasting.

86
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:45,120
This was before I knew we were doing the series or anything because I wanted, again, that level of intimacy with Jesus.

87
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:54,000
But I got about 12 hours into my fast and I got really irritated because I was like, I don't get this.

88
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,680
This does not make any sense.

89
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,760
Like, I'm really hungry.

90
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:58,580
I don't feel any closer to God.

91
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:01,700
My kids keep eating and they're annoying me that they're eating.

92
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:04,400
And I don't see the correlation.

93
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,740
Like, I'm just being totally honest with you.

94
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:13,480
I wanted to grow closer to God, but being hungry, it made no sense to me how you get from hunger drawing you close to Jesus.

95
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:18,420
And I'm one of those people that if it doesn't make sense to me, I'm going to figure it out or I'm not going to do it.

96
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:24,040
So I finished the fast out of a really bad heart set.

97
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:30,960
But I started to research and started to read and started to try to understand how fasting helps you grow closer to God.

98
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:38,180
And then about two months into that, Ryan told me we're doing this series and asked me if I would want to share a message with you.

99
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:41,520
And that's when I knew that God had been preparing me that whole time.

100
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:47,960
So the things that I was learning, I get to share with you this morning.

101
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:58,160
So those are the two questions I hope to answer this morning is how do we get to a place where Jesus is the highest priority, most important thing in our life?

102
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:00,580
And how does fasting help us get there?

103
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:07,100
So first off, if you've ever tried to fast, you know that fasting is a form of denying yourself, right?

104
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:10,380
You're really hungry, but you deny yourself food.

105
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:15,480
So let's look at what the Bible says and what Jesus specifically says about denying yourself.

106
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:27,460
If you look at Matthew 16, 24, Jesus says, whoever wants to be my disciple must deny themselves, take up their cross, and follow me.

107
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:29,720
A couple of really interesting things about this.

108
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:32,540
This is a pretty popular Scripture verse.

109
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:36,320
One thing that I found interesting is Jesus hadn't been crucified yet.

110
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:43,720
So the fact that he says, take up your cross and follow me, the disciples had to have been like, I mean, obviously they knew what crucifixion was,

111
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:48,680
but they didn't quite grasp that Jesus was going to die, and especially not on a cross.

112
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:50,480
So that probably didn't make a ton of sense to them.

113
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:58,880
But I want to go back a few Scripture verses before this, because it makes this make even more sense.

114
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:07,100
So if we look at Matthew 16, 21 through 24, it says,

115
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:32,080
So this is the first time he's told the disciples that his mission is to die and to be raised again.

116
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,300
So this had to have been shocking.

117
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:36,380
They're expecting, King of kings, Lord of lords, you're going to take over Rome.

118
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:38,300
We're going to be back in control.

119
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:42,960
And now he's telling them that his mission is to actually sacrifice his life.

120
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:47,300
Peter took him aside and began to rebuke him.

121
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:51,060
Never, Lord, he said, this shall never happen to you.

122
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:55,180
Jesus turned and said to Peter, get behind me, Satan.

123
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,920
You are a stumbling block to me.

124
00:09:57,920 --> 00:10:03,600
You do not have in mind the concerns of God, but merely human concerns.

125
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,560
Poor Peter.

126
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,980
That's not a fun thing for Jesus to call you.

127
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:12,140
And it's not, obviously, Peter wasn't possessed with Satan all of a sudden.

128
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:19,100
He, but Jesus was saying, this self-denial that I'm about to do, and it was a self-denial for Jesus.

129
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:24,180
He sweat droplets of blood hours before he was taken into custody.

130
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:27,440
He was going to feel every ounce of pain that you and I would have felt.

131
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:38,780
So he had strong urges to not feel that pain, but he knew in order to fulfill the mission, he had to deny himself and allow himself to be crucified.

132
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:51,380
So when Peter says, absolutely not, I won't let you, and he refers to him as Satan, he's saying, anything that's keeping me from fulfilling my mission, which is denying myself, is Satan's desire.

133
00:10:51,380 --> 00:11:04,440
Because who of all would want Jesus to not crucify himself on the cross, but Satan, because that division, the breakage between sin and God, is because Jesus sacrificed himself.

134
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:13,100
And then verse 24, it says, Jesus said to his disciples, whoever wants to be my disciple must deny himself, take up their cross, and follow me.

135
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:20,020
For whoever wants to save their life will lose it, but whoever loses their life for me will find it.

136
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:24,680
What good will it be for someone to gain the whole world, yet forfeit their soul?

137
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,640
Or what can anyone give in exchange for their soul?

138
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:35,400
For the Son of Man is going to come in his Father's glory with his angels, and then he will reward each person according to what they have done.

139
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:41,380
So Jesus is explaining what you think is good for man is not.

140
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:47,880
I'm telling you, if you really want good, you will deny yourself and follow me.

141
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:54,220
In reality, in our Western culture, we don't have very many ways that we have to deny ourselves, right?

142
00:11:54,220 --> 00:12:00,820
We see the stories of war going on in other countries and things like that, and they clearly have to deny themselves things all the time.

143
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:05,180
But here in America, we don't have too many ways we deny ourselves.

144
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:07,220
Actually, it's kind of the complete opposite.

145
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:14,240
Our world is wrapped up in this thing called what Freud, Freud knew everything, I'm just going to eat it.

146
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:19,640
Freud calls the pleasure principle, and that's what we're living on.

147
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:26,920
The pleasure principle is the instinctive seeking of physical and avoiding, of physical, I'm sorry.

148
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:34,740
The instinctive seeking of pleasure and avoiding of pain to satisfy biological and psychological needs.

149
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:39,740
In other words, focusing on doing what feels good in the moment.

150
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:42,320
That's what our culture pushes.

151
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,960
If it feels good, do it.

152
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,220
Don't worry about repercussions.

153
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,440
And it sounds good, right?

154
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:49,880
Like, that doesn't sound awful.

155
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:54,520
I think it's supposed to sound awful, because I'm saying it from here, but it doesn't sound awful.

156
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:55,920
Like, if it feels good, do it.

157
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:56,440
Why not?

158
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:57,040
Right?

159
00:12:57,100 --> 00:13:08,000
But we don't think about the effect that this has, because in reality, what feels good in the short term often reaps damage in the long term.

160
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:24,500
And more importantly, and what we're going to talk about today, is constantly supplying your body and mind with short-term earthly pleasures slowly quiets and eventually mutes the voice of God and the desire for heavenly things.

161
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:35,580
We've gotten so accustomed to filling every need immediately with an earthly pleasure that we have no more room for God to fill us.

162
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:36,180
Right?

163
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:45,220
Like, have you ever felt like you've gone through an entire day and, like, nothing really happened?

164
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:47,820
Like, you just, okay, I'm hungry, I eat.

165
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:49,940
I am sad about something.

166
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:57,040
I immediately turn on a show, or I listen to a song, or I, in my situation, call my mom, and she will make it better.

167
00:13:57,040 --> 00:14:02,800
Like, I don't, I just fill it immediately with whatever I can so that I don't have to feel anything.

168
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:11,740
And, at the end of the day, I didn't get any further along in my walk to be closer to God, because everything was filled with earthly things.

169
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:17,540
Have you ever got to a point in your relationship with God where you feel like you're knee-deep in water?

170
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:19,380
And you're like, is this it?

171
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:21,740
Is this as far as we get to go with Jesus?

172
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:25,240
Is this what Christianity is all about?

173
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:31,080
And I think a lot of that is because we don't leave room for Him to fill us.

174
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:36,300
And this is where the question of why fast comes into play.

175
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:50,140
Fasting is a tangible, practical way to deny yourself, as Jesus says, and wake up before we spend our entire lives going from one earthly pleasure to the next until we die.

176
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:51,680
Because that's Satan's goal.

177
00:14:51,680 --> 00:15:09,140
If he can keep us numb enough and filled enough in a false sense of fulfillment with earthly pleasures, to a point that we never let God infiltrate our lives or have any impact on us, until we die, we've remained lukewarm our entire lives.

178
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:29,640
We've remained knee-deep in this water that we think is all that Christianity has to offer when Jesus is saying, I have so much more to give you, but you won't give yourself a second to think and allow me to speak to you or allow me to fill those needs that you think you're filling with earthly things.

179
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:32,500
Because in reality, earthly things don't work, right?

180
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,400
We know that.

181
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:37,460
Even though we keep doing it, we know that these earthly things that we're trying don't help.

182
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:47,060
For example, I'm going to look at one of the easiest things that we do to bring ourselves pleasure, which can be, obviously, we need food, but then overeating.

183
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:53,720
Have you ever had one of those, like, I'm having an awful day and I'm just going to stuff myself silly because I don't care and it will make me happy?

184
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:58,160
Okay, so this is what happens to you when you overeat biologically.

185
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:04,320
Overeating causes the stomach to expand beyond its normal size to adjust to the large amounts of food.

186
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:08,620
The expanded stomach pushes against other organs, making you feel uncomfortable.

187
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:09,440
You felt that.

188
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,020
That's the, like, stuffed feeling.

189
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:16,060
This discomfort can take the form of feeling tired, sluggish, or drowsy.

190
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:19,940
Eating too much food requires your organs to work harder.

191
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:24,440
To break down the food, the stomach produces hydraulic acid, resulting in heartburn.

192
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:33,200
And metabolism may speed up as it tries to burn off those extra calories and you experience a temporary feeling of being hot, sweaty, or even dizzy.

193
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,800
Sorry, Ryan, I'm going to tell your story.

194
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:44,480
Ryan was, I was sharing this with him and he said that he remembers going to a Brazilian steakhouse and stuffing himself silly with all kinds of, like, red meat and stuff.

195
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,240
And then that night, he couldn't sleep.

196
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:53,280
He woke up and he was, like, drenched in sweat and dizzy and nauseous and all of that stuff.

197
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:57,580
That's because our bodies are not meant to take in that much at that pace.

198
00:16:57,580 --> 00:17:05,040
And then overeating can make it hard for you to sleep at night, which, if you don't have sleep, then the next morning you're grouchy and irritated.

199
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:13,340
Chronic overeating can produce obesity, insulin resistance, which increases your risk for heart attack, stroke, and diabetes.

200
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:22,780
So the more that you engage in these earthly pleasures to fill you, the further and further you get down this path of actually being happy.

201
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:23,720
It does the opposite.

202
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:30,380
And now, obviously, God has given us this earth and it is full of earthly pleasures for us to enjoy.

203
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:35,140
This is certainly not a, if you do anything that makes you happy, God's mad at you, message.

204
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:48,980
But it's when we do, when that is our only form of gaining happiness and we suck away the desire for Jesus because we fill it with this, that's what I'm talking about this morning.

205
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:55,880
And after a while, you start to feel depressed, anxious, and you can't put your finger on it, right?

206
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,520
You're like, nothing's really wrong.

207
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,480
Why am I so depressed?

208
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:00,800
Why can't I, why don't I want to get out of bed?

209
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:07,480
And this is the cycle that fulfilling these pleasure principles all the time brings you to.

210
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:13,300
We are often numb both to God and to our own lives.

211
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:14,700
And Jesus knows this.

212
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:17,000
He knows that this is what these pleasures are going to give us.

213
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:25,860
And so he's constantly telling us to wake up, to stay awake, to be vigilant, and to be alert to a deeper reality.

214
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:29,220
And this is what fasting does.

215
00:18:29,220 --> 00:18:33,780
Fasting is a spiritual practice that wakes us up.

216
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:36,280
It stops us in our track.

217
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:41,140
It stops us, because I'm telling you what, if you want to be awake, be hungry.

218
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:42,900
It's really hard to sleep.

219
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:49,520
And it stops you from fulfilling yourself with these earthly pleasures if you can't eat when you're hungry.

220
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:56,100
And it makes you stop and think, what is it that I'm doing with my life, and where does God actually want me to be?

221
00:18:56,660 --> 00:19:01,860
This morning, I was asked to talk to you about how fasting helps you grow in holiness.

222
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:09,460
Well, in order to do that, I want to explain what the word holiness means, because it's kind of an interesting biblical word.

223
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:10,300
So what does it mean?

224
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:21,400
If you look at Isaiah 6, 3, Isaiah was a prophet from the Old Testament, and he's just been given a mission by God, and he gets this mission through a vision.

225
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:27,000
So Isaiah gets to go into heaven in his vision, and he sees God sitting on his throne.

226
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:33,940
And there are serabim, which is like the highest of angels on both sides of him, and they're singing in loud voices,

227
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:37,980
Holy, holy, holy is the Lord of hosts.

228
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:42,680
That word holy, the repetition is not like we sing in a song.

229
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:47,820
It's emphasizing the fact that God is holy, holy, holy.

230
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:52,760
Think about it like if you went to like a weightlifting competition, and you were like, that guy over there is huge, huge, huge.

231
00:19:52,760 --> 00:20:02,600
Like, he's emphasizing it, that this is a really, really, really holy God, because he is the holiest of all.

232
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:08,260
The word holy comes from the Hebrew word kadash, which means to cut.

233
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:13,860
To be holy means to be cut off or separate from everything else.

234
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:21,460
It means to be in a class of your own, distinct from anything that has ever existed or will ever exist.

235
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:22,620
God is holy.

236
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:26,280
There is never going to be anything more holy than him.

237
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:33,080
He is in a class of his own, in a class that no one will ever surpass his holiness.

238
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:40,760
But what we don't think about very often is that because holiness is in the essence of God's character,

239
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:44,120
it becomes our calling as his children, too.

240
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:46,180
We are the apprentice of Jesus.

241
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:50,740
If Jesus is holy, we are called to be holy, which is such a weird concept.

242
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:55,520
But we are called to be set apart from the rest of the world.

243
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:59,440
Look at 1 Peter 1, 14 through 16.

244
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,600
It says,

245
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:06,520
As obedient children, do not conform to the evil desires you had when you lived in ignorance.

246
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:15,380
But just as he who called you is holy, so be holy in all you do.

247
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:19,140
For it is written, be holy, because I am holy.

248
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:24,280
We are called to be set apart in a class of our own.

249
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:29,180
Not because Jesus is mean and he wants us to not get to enjoy the earthly pleasures.

250
00:21:29,180 --> 00:21:32,360
He created the earth and all the pleasures that come with it.

251
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:39,020
But because he knows that these pleasures aren't going to work and that they're going to give us a fake sense of fulfillment.

252
00:21:39,020 --> 00:21:48,600
So he's trying to rescue us from getting in this cycle that we often get into where these pleasures give us this fake sense of fulfillment.

253
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:51,780
But this doesn't come naturally.

254
00:21:51,780 --> 00:22:00,260
We are going to constantly be pulled back to those earthly pleasures, which is why fasting is so important.

255
00:22:00,260 --> 00:22:06,720
Ryan talked last week about how fasting used to be something that all Christians did, or most.

256
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:12,000
If you wanted to reach a certain level with God, you fasted, usually once or twice a week.

257
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:19,060
And St. Leo the Great, who was the Bishop of Rome in the 5th century, describes fasting as this.

258
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:34,700
Fasting gives you strength against sin, represses evil desires, repels temptation, humbles pride, cools anger, and fosters all the inclinations of a goodwill, even unto the practice of every virtue.

259
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:40,400
That's a high standard for anything, to do all of these things.

260
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,600
So the question is, how?

261
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:45,320
How does fasting do all of these things?

262
00:22:45,320 --> 00:22:46,520
Because I want all of these.

263
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:51,780
I want to have, resist temptation and cool anger and humbles pride.

264
00:22:52,900 --> 00:23:00,480
So in our Western society, we often think of our relationship with God as just spiritual, or even in our minds, right?

265
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:03,680
So we read our Bible, we pray, we sing, we worship.

266
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:09,740
All of these things are spiritual or helping us grow in knowledge with God.

267
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:14,440
But we're forgetting something that's extremely important in our walk with God.

268
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:20,920
And I think this is why I was so confused how being hungry was going to help me grow closer to God, right?

269
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:24,220
Because I understand if I read my Bible, I get to know God.

270
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:25,820
He reveals himself to me in the Scriptures.

271
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:31,180
If I worship, if I go to church, if I do these things, it makes sense that my relationship with God will grow.

272
00:23:31,180 --> 00:23:36,100
But being hungry didn't make any sense to me whatsoever.

273
00:23:36,740 --> 00:23:42,320
However, this is not how the Bible describes our relationship with God and how it's supposed to be.

274
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:45,300
The Bible doesn't describe our relationship as merely spiritual.

275
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:48,460
In 1 Corinthians 6.19, it says,

276
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:53,760
Do you not know that your bodies are temples of the Holy Spirit?

277
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:55,920
Who is in you?

278
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:58,540
Whom you have received from God.

279
00:23:58,540 --> 00:24:00,700
What is a temple of the Holy Spirit?

280
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:03,620
Our bodies, our physical bodies.

281
00:24:03,620 --> 00:24:07,620
I grew up with the idea that your bodies really didn't mean anything, right?

282
00:24:07,620 --> 00:24:10,540
They were just what you have while on earth.

283
00:24:10,540 --> 00:24:13,620
And when you go to heaven, they'll be thrown away.

284
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:15,100
And your spirit is what lived on.

285
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:19,100
But the Bible makes it very clear that your bodies were not only created in God's image,

286
00:24:19,100 --> 00:24:21,660
created by God specifically for you,

287
00:24:21,660 --> 00:24:26,740
but they are also temples of the Holy Spirit.

288
00:24:28,220 --> 00:24:32,340
If your body is a temple for the Holy Spirit, then it should be easy to resist sin, right?

289
00:24:32,340 --> 00:24:33,880
Because he's living in us.

290
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:35,180
So this should be like an easy thing.

291
00:24:35,180 --> 00:24:36,280
We shouldn't even want to sin.

292
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:39,060
However, there's another side to the coin.

293
00:24:39,060 --> 00:24:41,360
Your body is also infected with sin,

294
00:24:41,360 --> 00:24:46,200
which is the part of you that's pulling you away from God constantly.

295
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:49,940
This is where the struggle comes into play.

296
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:57,080
Paul says it so clearly in this passage, but the word do is said so many times.

297
00:24:57,080 --> 00:24:57,940
So hang with me.

298
00:24:57,940 --> 00:25:00,700
It's a really hard passage to read, but it's really good.

299
00:25:00,700 --> 00:25:05,840
He talks about the struggle between wanting to do the will of God

300
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:08,800
and the struggle to your body wanting to sin.

301
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:12,780
So Romans 7, 15 through 24 says,

302
00:25:12,780 --> 00:25:16,760
I do not understand what I do.

303
00:25:16,760 --> 00:25:20,400
For what I want to do, I do not do.

304
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:23,160
But what I hate, I do.

305
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:27,660
For I know that good itself does not dwell in me.

306
00:25:27,660 --> 00:25:30,220
That is in my sinful nature.

307
00:25:30,220 --> 00:25:34,320
For I have the desire to do what is good, but I cannot carry it out.

308
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:38,100
For I do not do the good I want to do,

309
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:41,000
but the evil I do not want to do.

310
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:42,160
I told you so many do's.

311
00:25:42,160 --> 00:25:45,160
This I keep on doing, but we feel that, right?

312
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:48,840
Like I have the desire to do this good, but I just keep messing it up.

313
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:51,560
For in my inner being, I delight in God's law,

314
00:25:51,560 --> 00:25:54,580
but I see another law at work in me,

315
00:25:54,580 --> 00:25:58,600
raging war against the law of my mind

316
00:25:58,600 --> 00:26:03,520
and making me a prisoner of this law of sin at work within me.

317
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:05,720
What a wretched man I am.

318
00:26:05,720 --> 00:26:07,940
Who will rescue me from this body?

319
00:26:08,100 --> 00:26:09,740
That is subject to death.

320
00:26:09,740 --> 00:26:13,940
Like, couldn't say it better than this.

321
00:26:13,940 --> 00:26:16,780
What we want to do, we don't do.

322
00:26:16,780 --> 00:26:20,040
And what we don't want to do, we keep on doing.

323
00:26:20,040 --> 00:26:22,600
Have you guys ever seen those commercials of people on their cell phones?

324
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:24,140
They're like really depressing.

325
00:26:24,140 --> 00:26:25,940
Like the kids are trying to get their parents' attention

326
00:26:25,940 --> 00:26:28,140
and the parents are looking at their cell phones

327
00:26:28,140 --> 00:26:30,200
and then the couple's out on a date

328
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:32,500
and neither of them are talking because they're looking at their cell phones

329
00:26:32,500 --> 00:26:34,400
and it's saying like, stop looking at your cell phones.

330
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:37,700
And you're like, ugh, that's awful.

331
00:26:37,700 --> 00:26:39,860
I am not going to look at my cell phone.

332
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:41,760
I'm going to focus on my children

333
00:26:41,760 --> 00:26:43,940
and I'm going to look at my husband

334
00:26:43,940 --> 00:26:46,180
and I'm putting my phone down

335
00:26:46,180 --> 00:26:47,440
and then 20 minutes later,

336
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:48,900
your phone goes off

337
00:26:48,900 --> 00:26:50,820
and you look at text message

338
00:26:50,820 --> 00:26:51,960
and then you go on Facebook

339
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,320
and then you go on Yahoo

340
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,780
and you're like, oh, shoot.

341
00:26:54,780 --> 00:26:57,080
It was 20 minutes of me not looking at my phone

342
00:26:57,080 --> 00:26:59,540
and I'm already back to doing the exact same thing.

343
00:26:59,540 --> 00:27:02,160
What I want to do, I don't do.

344
00:27:02,160 --> 00:27:03,940
What I do not want to do, I keep on doing it.

345
00:27:03,940 --> 00:27:05,520
And that's what Paul's saying.

346
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:09,760
We are constantly being pulled back to these sinful desires.

347
00:27:09,760 --> 00:27:16,060
Because our body is the temple of the Holy Spirit,

348
00:27:16,060 --> 00:27:19,220
but we are also fighting this sin.

349
00:27:19,220 --> 00:27:22,540
The sin part of us, Paul refers to as flesh.

350
00:27:22,540 --> 00:27:26,700
The flesh is the part of you that drives you towards food,

351
00:27:26,900 --> 00:27:30,480
laziness, lust, instant gratification, power, control,

352
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:34,060
and it pulls us away from the things that God has from us.

353
00:27:34,060 --> 00:27:39,440
But our fight is not against our body.

354
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:43,080
This is not a message about self-torture.

355
00:27:43,080 --> 00:27:44,840
You're not supposed to beat up your body

356
00:27:44,840 --> 00:27:46,520
so that it will align right with God.

357
00:27:46,520 --> 00:27:48,400
It's actually for your body.

358
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:50,900
It is against that flesh,

359
00:27:50,900 --> 00:27:54,640
that sinful nature that pulls us away from God.

360
00:27:54,640 --> 00:27:59,100
So how do we starve our flesh and feed our spirit?

361
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:02,680
Well, I said before that we're apprentices of Jesus, right?

362
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:04,640
So we need to look at what Jesus did

363
00:28:04,640 --> 00:28:07,440
and draw on the power of the Holy Spirit like he did.

364
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:13,200
Fasting is an essential practice that helps us crucify our flesh

365
00:28:13,200 --> 00:28:18,160
and bring our bodies back into an alignment with God that dwells within us.

366
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:22,200
Think of it like this, and this is probably the best way I can explain it.

367
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:29,300
Fasting is a way to train your body to be in an alignment with your spirit.

368
00:28:29,300 --> 00:28:30,520
Do we have any runners here?

369
00:28:30,600 --> 00:28:31,240
I know we have Shauna.

370
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:31,740
Where's Shauna?

371
00:28:31,740 --> 00:28:34,380
Well, she used to be a runner.

372
00:28:34,380 --> 00:28:35,120
No, the other one.

373
00:28:35,120 --> 00:28:35,640
Sorry.

374
00:28:35,640 --> 00:28:37,260
Corn.

375
00:28:37,260 --> 00:28:38,500
It's multiple Shaunas.

376
00:28:38,500 --> 00:28:41,960
She used to be a runner, and then I made her break her ankle.

377
00:28:41,960 --> 00:28:42,820
She must...

378
00:28:42,820 --> 00:28:43,460
I don't know where she is.

379
00:28:43,460 --> 00:28:46,400
Anyways, she fell at a kid's event and broke her ankle.

380
00:28:46,400 --> 00:28:46,980
It was really bad.

381
00:28:46,980 --> 00:28:48,600
But she runs like 50-mile races.

382
00:28:48,980 --> 00:28:52,880
If you are a runner, you know you cannot get up one morning

383
00:28:52,880 --> 00:28:56,020
and go to a marathon and run 26.2 miles.

384
00:28:56,020 --> 00:28:58,840
That's how the word marathon came to be.

385
00:28:58,840 --> 00:29:03,720
The first guy that ran 26.2 miles died on the spot when he got at the end of it.

386
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:06,020
You can't do that.

387
00:29:06,020 --> 00:29:07,720
Your body hasn't been trained, right?

388
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:08,920
You have to start slow.

389
00:29:08,920 --> 00:29:10,200
It's not fun.

390
00:29:10,200 --> 00:29:12,340
If you've ever started running and you're not a runner,

391
00:29:12,340 --> 00:29:14,920
you know it's miserable.

392
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:17,280
Every part of you wants to stop.

393
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:21,420
And then for weeks later, your body's mad at you for what you put it through

394
00:29:21,420 --> 00:29:23,200
in that one-whole-mile run.

395
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:25,160
But it takes time.

396
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:26,660
You have to train.

397
00:29:26,660 --> 00:29:28,960
You have to start small, work big.

398
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:30,660
My daughter's a gymnast.

399
00:29:30,660 --> 00:29:32,640
She's actually at a meet right now.

400
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:35,320
So, like, internally, I'm nervous for her there, too.

401
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:37,340
But I have this...

402
00:29:37,340 --> 00:29:38,640
I've been to so many of her meets.

403
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:41,360
She's in the gym 16 hours a week every single week.

404
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:46,460
And I have this recurring dream that I am on her team.

405
00:29:46,740 --> 00:29:49,880
And so I get up to the balance beam, and it's my turn.

406
00:29:49,880 --> 00:29:52,980
And I'm like, I can't do this.

407
00:29:52,980 --> 00:29:54,920
And the coach is like, go.

408
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:55,640
It's your turn.

409
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:57,800
And I can't even do a cartwheel on regular ground,

410
00:29:57,800 --> 00:29:59,880
let alone a back handspring on a little tiny beam.

411
00:29:59,880 --> 00:30:03,040
And I just remember being terrified that I'm like,

412
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:05,440
I have no idea what to do.

413
00:30:05,440 --> 00:30:06,760
I can't even stand on this thing and thing.

414
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:08,380
Because I haven't trained.

415
00:30:08,380 --> 00:30:12,700
McKinley is 11, and she can do these things that I could never do

416
00:30:12,700 --> 00:30:15,200
because of the amount of training that she's gone into.

417
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:19,280
That's what fasting does for you and I.

418
00:30:19,280 --> 00:30:23,480
It is a training tool to train our bodies

419
00:30:23,480 --> 00:30:29,260
to be able to be in pain and still rely on God.

420
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:36,500
This is the most important part that I hope that I'm able to portray to you.

421
00:30:38,660 --> 00:30:44,380
If we can train our bodies that we are okay feeling in discomfort

422
00:30:44,380 --> 00:30:48,440
and we still lean on God in our discomfort,

423
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:51,700
it translates to the rest of our lives.

424
00:30:51,700 --> 00:30:55,380
If in this moment I chose not to eat and I was okay

425
00:30:55,380 --> 00:30:57,660
and God was still there for me,

426
00:30:57,660 --> 00:31:02,060
it translates into I'm having a moment where I'm in need

427
00:31:02,060 --> 00:31:04,440
or I have no patience for this

428
00:31:04,440 --> 00:31:06,360
or God's not answering this prayer.

429
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:08,720
We go back to the feeling that we had when we were in fasting

430
00:31:08,720 --> 00:31:11,500
and we're like, okay, I can have patience

431
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:13,920
because in this moment I wasn't feeling great,

432
00:31:13,920 --> 00:31:15,100
but God got me through it.

433
00:31:15,100 --> 00:31:18,500
In this moment in real life, I'm not loving how this is going,

434
00:31:18,500 --> 00:31:19,900
but God's getting me through it.

435
00:31:19,900 --> 00:31:23,460
And I'm going to tell you four steps on how you get there,

436
00:31:23,460 --> 00:31:24,960
but first, quick recap.

437
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:28,020
Number one, we are called to deny ourselves

438
00:31:28,020 --> 00:31:30,380
because the Savior of the world denied himself

439
00:31:30,380 --> 00:31:32,100
all the way to the cross.

440
00:31:32,100 --> 00:31:35,300
And he asks us to deny ourselves,

441
00:31:35,300 --> 00:31:37,520
not because he's mean and he wants to keep us

442
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:38,500
from the things of this world,

443
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:41,740
but because he knows the things of this world do not work.

444
00:31:41,740 --> 00:31:44,640
They give us a false sense of fullness,

445
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:48,900
which is why we're left depressed and anxious and worried

446
00:31:48,900 --> 00:31:50,440
and we can't figure out why.

447
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:52,960
We are called to be set apart.

448
00:31:52,960 --> 00:31:55,600
We are called to be holy because God is holy.

449
00:31:55,600 --> 00:31:58,260
So we are called to do things differently

450
00:31:58,260 --> 00:32:00,100
than the rest of the world.

451
00:32:00,100 --> 00:32:04,060
We have two desires pulling at us.

452
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:06,000
We have our fleshly sinful desire

453
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:09,340
that is pulling us towards all the temptations of the world.

454
00:32:09,340 --> 00:32:10,620
And then we have our spirit,

455
00:32:10,620 --> 00:32:13,880
which knows that we need to be close to Jesus

456
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:17,340
and we need to lean on him for these desires that we have.

457
00:32:17,340 --> 00:32:22,060
And then finally, fasting is a way to train our bodies,

458
00:32:22,060 --> 00:32:24,840
just like reading Scripture trains your spirit,

459
00:32:24,840 --> 00:32:27,860
just like worship draws you closer to God.

460
00:32:27,860 --> 00:32:30,520
Fasting is a way to train your body

461
00:32:30,520 --> 00:32:33,340
to line up with your spirit as well.

462
00:32:33,340 --> 00:32:34,760
And here's how it works.

463
00:32:34,760 --> 00:32:41,160
Number one, fasting weans you off the pleasure principle.

464
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:43,600
Talked about the pleasure principle a lot,

465
00:32:43,600 --> 00:32:46,320
that it's that desire to do what feels good in the moment,

466
00:32:46,320 --> 00:32:48,100
no matter what the consequences are.

467
00:32:48,100 --> 00:32:50,500
Fasting doesn't allow you to do this.

468
00:32:50,500 --> 00:32:51,340
When you're fasting,

469
00:32:51,340 --> 00:32:54,960
you have to constantly resist this urge

470
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:57,700
and remain hungry, right?

471
00:32:57,700 --> 00:33:00,640
It is a way for us to deny ourselves

472
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:03,260
when we normally have no need to deny ourselves.

473
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:07,360
We have to learn to be okay with being hungry.

474
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:13,080
You are teaching yourself that you can do the right thing,

475
00:33:13,080 --> 00:33:14,780
even if it's hard.

476
00:33:14,780 --> 00:33:17,580
So that feeling of hunger that you get

477
00:33:17,580 --> 00:33:18,520
when you're like, this is stupid,

478
00:33:18,520 --> 00:33:20,120
I just want to eat, this isn't helping at all.

479
00:33:20,120 --> 00:33:23,440
It's teaching your body that even when things are hard,

480
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:26,080
you can resist it and you can keep going.

481
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:26,980
This is temporary.

482
00:33:26,980 --> 00:33:29,000
Isn't that how things go in life?

483
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:31,200
It feels like it's never going to end.

484
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:33,400
And when you have 12 more hours of not eating,

485
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:35,200
it's going to feel like it's never going to end.

486
00:33:35,200 --> 00:33:35,940
But it does.

487
00:33:35,940 --> 00:33:38,080
And when you get to the end

488
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:41,200
and you've allowed God to get you through a hard time,

489
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:44,720
you realize it translates into other aspects of your life.

490
00:33:44,820 --> 00:33:48,340
I can get through this because I know in the end God's got me.

491
00:33:48,340 --> 00:33:52,520
I can get through this because I know that this is a training tool

492
00:33:52,520 --> 00:33:53,740
that God's going to use.

493
00:33:53,740 --> 00:33:56,300
So don't lean on the earthly pleasures.

494
00:33:56,300 --> 00:34:00,380
Give it to God and allow yourself to feel a little bit of discomfort

495
00:34:00,380 --> 00:34:01,980
in order for Jesus.

496
00:34:04,780 --> 00:34:08,060
In time, your ability to overcome your fleshly desires

497
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:11,040
will begin to teach you how to be happy and content

498
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:13,120
when you don't get what you want.

499
00:34:13,120 --> 00:34:18,060
That is a lesson that is so important for all of us to learn,

500
00:34:18,060 --> 00:34:18,800
especially me.

501
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:21,400
If things don't go the way that I want,

502
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:25,120
I can still be content in Jesus.

503
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:28,000
If I'm hungry and I'm not getting what I want,

504
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,220
which is immediate gratification,

505
00:34:29,220 --> 00:34:33,060
I can still worship God and lean on God,

506
00:34:33,060 --> 00:34:34,580
even in my discomfort,

507
00:34:34,580 --> 00:34:37,400
not rushing to fix it.

508
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:40,340
I am a rusher to fix things.

509
00:34:40,340 --> 00:34:43,140
Fasting, you can't make that time speed up.

510
00:34:43,140 --> 00:34:45,780
You're either going to follow through with what God asked you to do

511
00:34:45,780 --> 00:34:46,680
or you're not.

512
00:34:46,680 --> 00:34:47,920
It's not going to speed up.

513
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:51,000
You have to have patience and you have to endure it

514
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:54,200
and then you reach the end of that.

515
00:34:54,200 --> 00:34:56,780
You can have like the best meal you want at the end of that if you want.

516
00:34:56,780 --> 00:35:00,880
What Paul says in Philippians 4, 11 through 13,

517
00:35:00,880 --> 00:35:04,160
I'm not saying this because I am in need

518
00:35:04,160 --> 00:35:09,140
for I have learned to be content in whatever the circumstances.

519
00:35:09,140 --> 00:35:11,860
I know what it is to be in need

520
00:35:11,860 --> 00:35:13,820
and I know what it is to have plenty.

521
00:35:13,820 --> 00:35:18,980
I have learned the secret of being content in any and every situation,

522
00:35:18,980 --> 00:35:21,220
whether well-fed or hungry,

523
00:35:21,220 --> 00:35:23,620
whether living in plenty or in want,

524
00:35:23,620 --> 00:35:28,520
I can do all things through Christ who gives me strength.

525
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:31,400
Not the world, not food,

526
00:35:31,400 --> 00:35:33,760
not my mom who answers the phone

527
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:35,760
and helps me get through whatever travesty I'm in.

528
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:39,220
Christ giving us strength.

529
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:41,680
We are learning to depend on Him.

530
00:35:41,680 --> 00:35:43,220
Paul says over and over again,

531
00:35:43,220 --> 00:35:44,960
I have learned this.

532
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:46,260
You don't have many...

533
00:35:46,260 --> 00:35:47,640
Think of the life that Paul led.

534
00:35:47,640 --> 00:35:48,800
He was imprisoned.

535
00:35:49,180 --> 00:35:50,060
He was beaten.

536
00:35:50,060 --> 00:35:51,680
He was...

537
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:55,120
I mean like he learned how to lean on God.

538
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:59,200
We don't go through those things on a daily basis.

539
00:35:59,200 --> 00:36:04,160
So fasting is our way to feel discomfort and still lean on God.

540
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:10,320
Remember that fasting is a training tool, right?

541
00:36:10,320 --> 00:36:13,460
It's a tool to help you get to the point where you're leaning on God.

542
00:36:13,460 --> 00:36:17,520
What starts as finding happiness even when you're hungry

543
00:36:17,520 --> 00:36:20,960
begins to translate into all other areas of your life.

544
00:36:20,960 --> 00:36:23,640
When we can't get what we want due to life circumstances

545
00:36:23,640 --> 00:36:26,080
or when other people's decisions upset us

546
00:36:26,080 --> 00:36:29,860
or even when God's sovereignty and His appointment over our lives

547
00:36:29,860 --> 00:36:31,860
doesn't go the way we expected it to go,

548
00:36:32,260 --> 00:36:36,260
we are increasingly free of anger and anxiety

549
00:36:36,260 --> 00:36:39,220
and are instead filled with joy and peace.

550
00:36:39,220 --> 00:36:40,520
That's what we want, right?

551
00:36:40,520 --> 00:36:43,000
That we think those earthly pleasures are going to give us.

552
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:44,160
But they don't work.

553
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:48,920
But this tool of denying yourself and allowing Christ to fill you

554
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:53,420
will help you be increasingly free of anger, anxiety,

555
00:36:53,420 --> 00:36:55,440
and filled with joy and peace.

556
00:36:55,440 --> 00:37:00,220
So I told you my first fasting experience.

557
00:37:00,220 --> 00:37:01,160
I was just mostly mad.

558
00:37:02,260 --> 00:37:03,840
I kept doing it.

559
00:37:03,840 --> 00:37:04,740
It was like once a week.

560
00:37:04,740 --> 00:37:09,220
And so I can remember distinctly a time when I was, again,

561
00:37:09,220 --> 00:37:11,180
probably like 15 hours into a fast.

562
00:37:11,180 --> 00:37:12,780
And I had made my kids bread.

563
00:37:12,780 --> 00:37:15,000
Because as a mom, it doesn't matter if you're not eating.

564
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,720
Everybody else in your family still has to eat.

565
00:37:16,720 --> 00:37:18,080
So I made them bread.

566
00:37:18,080 --> 00:37:19,960
And it's these rolls that are so good.

567
00:37:19,960 --> 00:37:20,960
And they smell so good.

568
00:37:20,960 --> 00:37:23,460
And they just come out of the oven.

569
00:37:23,460 --> 00:37:25,420
And I wanted to eat one so bad.

570
00:37:25,420 --> 00:37:32,740
And I can remember feeling the Holy Spirit saying to me clearly in that moment,

571
00:37:32,740 --> 00:37:35,260
you have a choice to make right now.

572
00:37:35,260 --> 00:37:39,080
You can choose the easy way out, like you usually do.

573
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:40,760
And you can grab that bread.

574
00:37:40,760 --> 00:37:43,440
And it's going to make you feel better for a few seconds.

575
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:48,300
Or you can choose to follow me, even if it doesn't make sense.

576
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:50,740
Even if it's not what you want.

577
00:37:50,740 --> 00:37:53,400
Even if it's not going to cause immediate gratification,

578
00:37:53,400 --> 00:37:55,120
which is what you usually search for.

579
00:37:55,120 --> 00:37:59,600
And that translates into the rest of my life.

580
00:37:59,600 --> 00:38:02,100
I could think of so many instances in that moment

581
00:38:02,100 --> 00:38:05,700
where I had made the wrong choices in other things.

582
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:07,580
I had gone for the immediate gratification.

583
00:38:07,580 --> 00:38:13,800
And these quick, earthly things that I usually would grab for,

584
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:17,780
like the bread, are constantly making me numb.

585
00:38:17,780 --> 00:38:21,480
And they're holding me back from a deeper relationship with Jesus

586
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:24,240
that he desperately wants to have with me.

587
00:38:24,240 --> 00:38:26,780
Where he fills those needs.

588
00:38:26,780 --> 00:38:28,660
Not earthly bread.

589
00:38:28,660 --> 00:38:31,160
That's why Jesus said, I am the bread of life.

590
00:38:31,160 --> 00:38:35,220
And that verse just blaringly obvious to me in that moment.

591
00:38:35,220 --> 00:38:38,380
You keep going to these small things

592
00:38:38,380 --> 00:38:43,920
when I want to give you so much more than you could ever imagine.

593
00:38:45,260 --> 00:38:53,300
After that experience, I started to feel myself react to things differently.

594
00:38:53,300 --> 00:38:57,280
It was the craziest thing because it kind of came out of nowhere.

595
00:38:57,280 --> 00:39:03,440
I could feel my desires to fix my problems immediately start to come down.

596
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:07,340
And I could feel my ability to wait on God increase.

597
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:12,820
I told Pastor Ryan that at one point I was in my car and the worship music came on.

598
00:39:12,820 --> 00:39:19,060
And my connection with Jesus felt so much stronger than it had before

599
00:39:19,060 --> 00:39:24,920
because he was filling me where I didn't allow him to do so before.

600
00:39:25,720 --> 00:39:29,240
And then I began to have peace in areas that I never used to have peace.

601
00:39:29,240 --> 00:39:35,160
I had an interaction with a friend of mine who had confronted me.

602
00:39:35,160 --> 00:39:37,640
She felt like I could have handled a situation better.

603
00:39:37,640 --> 00:39:40,740
My immediate reaction in those situations are,

604
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:47,700
like kind of want to like crawl up in a hole and die slash justify myself, right?

605
00:39:47,700 --> 00:39:48,660
Anybody else there?

606
00:39:48,660 --> 00:39:50,840
Somebody says you could have handled this differently

607
00:39:50,840 --> 00:39:53,820
and you want to think of 15 reasons why they could have handled it differently.

608
00:39:53,820 --> 00:39:56,040
And it was probably not my fault.

609
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:57,480
Also, I'm really embarrassed.

610
00:39:57,480 --> 00:40:04,180
But in that moment, I felt the peace of God surround me.

611
00:40:04,320 --> 00:40:06,500
And I was able to listen and be like,

612
00:40:06,500 --> 00:40:08,320
yeah, I probably could have handled that differently.

613
00:40:08,320 --> 00:40:09,480
I'm really sorry.

614
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:11,620
And then the craziest thing was,

615
00:40:11,620 --> 00:40:15,600
I walked away and it didn't haunt me for the next five days.

616
00:40:15,600 --> 00:40:16,880
Because that's how I work.

617
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:18,580
It sits in my gut, in my heart.

618
00:40:18,580 --> 00:40:21,300
And I'm like, I think of all the ways that they messed up

619
00:40:21,300 --> 00:40:22,480
and I could have done this or like,

620
00:40:22,480 --> 00:40:23,900
and it sits with me.

621
00:40:23,900 --> 00:40:26,640
And I walked away and I kept expecting it to hit me.

622
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:30,000
And I expected myself to be irritated and it never came.

623
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:33,060
It was literally insane for me.

624
00:40:33,060 --> 00:40:34,200
It was life-changing.

625
00:40:34,200 --> 00:40:37,520
And I knew it was because God was using

626
00:40:37,520 --> 00:40:40,700
the way that I was able to deny myself

627
00:40:40,700 --> 00:40:42,200
and lean on Him in that moment

628
00:40:42,200 --> 00:40:44,500
to actually step back and be like,

629
00:40:44,500 --> 00:40:47,100
no, I actually could have handled that differently

630
00:40:47,100 --> 00:40:47,840
and I'm really sorry.

631
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:48,960
And then let it go.

632
00:40:48,960 --> 00:40:52,360
And have peace that I rarely have

633
00:40:52,360 --> 00:40:54,300
in situations like that.

634
00:40:54,300 --> 00:41:00,320
Number two, fasting reveals what's in our hearts.

635
00:41:01,320 --> 00:41:05,640
Often we have a very misleading idea of how strong we are.

636
00:41:05,640 --> 00:41:08,460
Some of us have this concept of like,

637
00:41:08,460 --> 00:41:09,840
I got this.

638
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:11,720
This is not going to be hard at all

639
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:13,260
because I'm going to lean on the power of Jesus

640
00:41:13,260 --> 00:41:15,920
and I'm not even going to be hungry for the next 24 hours.

641
00:41:15,920 --> 00:41:19,860
Fasting is really good at humbling you

642
00:41:19,860 --> 00:41:23,280
and making you realize we're not quite as strong

643
00:41:23,280 --> 00:41:24,980
as we think that we are.

644
00:41:25,040 --> 00:41:27,520
And we aren't that good at sacrificing for Jesus

645
00:41:27,520 --> 00:41:31,120
because we really don't have to all that much.

646
00:41:32,180 --> 00:41:35,840
We start to realize how much we need earthly pleasures

647
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:37,720
to be happy, right?

648
00:41:37,720 --> 00:41:40,040
We think, I'm all filled with Jesus.

649
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,660
I don't need earthly pleasures.

650
00:41:41,660 --> 00:41:43,500
He and I are going to get this together.

651
00:41:43,500 --> 00:41:46,100
15 hours in, you're like, you know what?

652
00:41:46,100 --> 00:41:46,720
This is stupid.

653
00:41:46,720 --> 00:41:47,960
I don't need to fast.

654
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:49,320
I'm just going to go back

655
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:51,000
and me and Jesus will talk this out later,

656
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:51,720
but this is dumb.

657
00:41:51,920 --> 00:41:55,660
Because we realize how weak we really are

658
00:41:55,660 --> 00:41:58,280
and how much we depend on other things

659
00:41:58,280 --> 00:42:01,120
that aren't Jesus to get us through this.

660
00:42:01,120 --> 00:42:03,280
This is a good thing.

661
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:05,080
Don't fight that.

662
00:42:05,080 --> 00:42:08,160
If this is something you choose to partake in

663
00:42:08,160 --> 00:42:09,420
and you start to feel that,

664
00:42:09,420 --> 00:42:13,560
don't be ashamed of what you're feeling.

665
00:42:13,560 --> 00:42:15,700
Rather, acknowledge your weakness

666
00:42:15,700 --> 00:42:16,900
and give it to God.

667
00:42:16,900 --> 00:42:19,500
One of the very best ways you can come

668
00:42:19,500 --> 00:42:22,940
to the foot of the cross is at complete humility.

669
00:42:22,940 --> 00:42:24,640
The Bible talks about how Jesus says,

670
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:26,780
come to me like the children come to me.

671
00:42:26,780 --> 00:42:29,420
It's not because the children are like his favorite.

672
00:42:29,420 --> 00:42:30,920
It's because the children don't have

673
00:42:30,920 --> 00:42:32,620
high expectations of themselves.

674
00:42:32,620 --> 00:42:35,600
They come to Jesus knowing they're not worthy.

675
00:42:35,600 --> 00:42:39,540
We often come to him thinking we're kind of on par

676
00:42:39,540 --> 00:42:41,320
and we're at the same level

677
00:42:41,320 --> 00:42:43,340
until we put ourselves through something like this.

678
00:42:43,340 --> 00:42:46,960
And then it's astonishing how weak we really are.

679
00:42:47,620 --> 00:42:50,920
This is one of my absolute favorite quotes for today,

680
00:42:50,920 --> 00:42:51,580
but it says,

681
00:42:51,580 --> 00:42:55,300
as we come to God and give him our weakness,

682
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:59,040
he comes to us and gives us his strength.

683
00:42:59,040 --> 00:43:03,020
That's what I experienced that day with the confrontation.

684
00:43:03,020 --> 00:43:06,920
I had given him my weakness during the fasting

685
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:11,040
and he gave me his strength in that conversation.

686
00:43:11,040 --> 00:43:13,980
And I've never experienced that before.

687
00:43:13,980 --> 00:43:16,380
And it was worth every second of discomfort

688
00:43:16,380 --> 00:43:18,360
during those fasting hours.

689
00:43:18,360 --> 00:43:22,600
Number three, fasting reorders our desires.

690
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:26,700
One of the most astonishing I found through my fast

691
00:43:26,700 --> 00:43:29,100
is my desires started to shift.

692
00:43:29,100 --> 00:43:33,340
Not only was I able to not go to earthly pleasures

693
00:43:33,340 --> 00:43:36,140
like filling myself with shows

694
00:43:36,140 --> 00:43:38,540
or calling someone to help me get through something,

695
00:43:38,540 --> 00:43:42,140
but I actually wanted to go to Jesus,

696
00:43:42,140 --> 00:43:45,380
which was, again, astonishing to me.

697
00:43:45,380 --> 00:43:46,880
I didn't know that the fasting

698
00:43:46,880 --> 00:43:48,620
was going to do these things in my life,

699
00:43:48,620 --> 00:43:50,360
but when I started to feel them,

700
00:43:50,360 --> 00:43:51,760
I knew where they were coming from.

701
00:43:51,760 --> 00:43:53,600
I could sit in my car.

702
00:43:53,600 --> 00:43:55,320
Typically, I am a,

703
00:43:55,320 --> 00:43:57,640
if I'm in my car, I need music on

704
00:43:57,640 --> 00:43:58,900
or I need to call someone.

705
00:43:58,900 --> 00:44:00,720
Does anybody else have that like extreme urge

706
00:44:00,720 --> 00:44:01,860
